  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "645828dc6c05d4d2b275c97e2ea84c527d4f9321",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 834201174,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I wonder if the tvb functions themselves can be made robust against, in this case, datalen is 0 and adding a NULL string? I.e.\n\ntvb_new_subset_length() returns NULL when datalen == 0\n\ntvb_composite_append() NOP for tvb ==  NULL\n\nThis instead of going through all dissectors and put in guards against misuse. Somewhat the same as when we moved the checks for tree == NULL into the proto_tree functions. It cleaned up the dissector code quite nicely.\n\nNot sure if this is possible in this case, but something to consider.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/722b0c520542a23cb8f8ea7070a45c88f9e9214dc700ac151e419e9649e0304e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/JaapKeuter"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-02-07T12:16:27.517Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-02-07T16:53:48.302Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 138896290,
